what began as a family party now  described as a national tragedy  Flames tore through this home in the  densely populated gebalia refugee camp  in Northern gaza's strip  neighbors say they could hear screaming  but the fire was so intense they  couldn't help those trapped inside  I was sleeping in the living room that  looks out to my neighbors I was asleep  with my five-year-old and I heard people  screaming so I woke up  our brothers in the civil defense  arrived tried to enter the apartment but  couldn't they had no masks and no oxygen  tanks and the people burned inside and  until that moment we still didn't go  even one meter into the apartment the  dead are all believed to be of the  aburaya family they were gathering to  celebrate a birthday and welcoming home  their father who obtained a PhD overseas  but now their home is just a wreck of  charred walls and black suits  there was a large amount of fuel on  location which acted as a fire hazard  teams of firefighters quickly rushed to  the scene and the civil defense opened  an immediate investigation  the civil defense teams face great  difficulty in containing the enormous  fire a large number of fire brigade  officers and Palestinian police rushed  to the scene and had to use a lot of  equipment to put out the flames and to  prevent it from spreading to neighboring  homes and areas  those who survived the blaze have been  rushed to local hospitals Israel  maintains a blockade of Gaza but says it  will help those in need of medical  treatment  Palestinian president Mahmoud Abbas says  the victims will be remembered with the  day of national Mourning  you see it Al Jazeera gazda
 

